<title>GERMANY: Praktiker 95/96 oper profit falls.</title>
<headline>Praktiker 95/96 oper profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities	201.8 vs 220.4</p>
<p>    Group DVFA earnings/share		2.11    vs 2.34 DM</p>
<p>    Group sales				  4,250   up 4.5 pct</p>
<p>    Dividend				     1.90    vs 1.90 DM</p>
<p>NOTE - Metro AG unit Praktiker Bau- und Heimwerkermaerkte AG said its group income from ordinary activities in the first quarter of the current fiscal year was 36.3 million marks, about 16 million marks less than in the year-earlier quarter, and that it would have difficulty matching last year's results for the full year.</p>
<p>Sales rose 5.4 percent in the quarter, but on a same-store basis they were down 7.9 percent.</p>
<p>Six new stores were opened during the quarter.</p>
<p>On a same-stores basis, 1995/96 sales were down 5.5 percent. Praktiker opened nine new stores and closed one store during 1995/96.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
